"""Vishay WSK2512, 5 mOhm to 0.2 Ohm - 4-terminal (Kelvin) Power Metal Strip current-sense
resistor, 2512 (6332 metric), 1 W. Bare part.

Datasheet: Vishay Dale WSK2512, document 30108, revision 11-Dec-2023.

Why a package per resistance band: the WSK2512 terminal length T and the recommended land
pattern depend on the resistance (Dimensions and Solder Pad Dimensions tables): T 1.19 mm with
force pads a = 2.29 mm, l = 3.68 mm apart for 0.005 to 0.2 Ohm; T 2.21 mm (0.001-0.0049 Ohm) or
2.66 mm (0.0005-0.00099 Ohm) with a = 3.30 mm, l = 1.65 mm below. This package is the 0.005 to
0.2 Ohm band; `vishay/WSK2512-MID` is 0.001 to 0.0049 Ohm.

Part number (Global Part Number Information): WSK2512 + value + tolerance + packaging.
Value: R0100 = 0.0100 Ohm, 5L000 = 5.000 mOhm ("L" for values below 0.01 Ohm). Tolerance F = 1 %,
D = 0.5 %, B = 0.1 %. EA = lead-free tape and reel (2000 per 7" reel, Packaging table).
Selectable parts (`mpn`), each on LCSC (queried 2026-10-15):
- WSK2512R0100FEA: 10 mOhm 1 % (default; LCSC C3985410).
- WSK2512R0100DEA: 10 mOhm 0.5 % (LCSC C1517461). Same footprint, same TCR; only the initial
  tolerance differs.
- WSK25125L000FEA: 5 mOhm 1 % (LCSC C1517444), for a motor peak above the 10 mOhm range.

Ratings (Standard Electrical Specifications, Technical Specifications):
- Power 1.0 W at 70 C, derated linearly to 0 at 170 C (Derating figure); maximum working voltage
  (P x R)^0.5 (0.1 V at 10 mOhm, so 10 A continuous at 70 C).
- TCR +-35 ppm/C for 0.005 to 0.2 Ohm (+-75 ppm/C at 3-4.9 mOhm, +-250 ppm/C at 1-2.9 mOhm).
- Tolerance 1 % from 0.0005 Ohm, 0.5 % from 0.001 Ohm, 0.1 % from 0.01 Ohm.
- Operating temperature -65 to +170 C; inductance 0.5 to 5 nH (Features); AEC-Q200.
- Thermal EMF: doc 30108 gives none; Vishay's Power Metal Strip product overview (VMN-PL0407-1703,
  2017, p7), which lists the WSK2512, states that the series "utilize resistance materials that
  have low thermal EMF characteristics (below 3 uV/C)". With a Kelvin part the EMFs of the two
  ends cancel but for their temperature difference: 3 uV/C x 2 C is 0.6 mA at 10 mOhm.
- Stability (Performance table): load life, 1000 h at rated power and 70 C, +-(1.0 % + 0.5 mOhm);
  thermal shock +-(0.5 % + 0.5 mOhm).

Terminals (Electrical Connection figure): I1 and I2 carry the current, E1 and E2 are the voltage
sense connections. E1 is the sense finger of the I1 end, E2 of the I2 end. Pads (footprint and
KiCad's Device:R_Shunt numbering): 1 I1, 2 E1 (left end), 3 E2, 4 I2 (right end).

io: P1/P2 are the force (current) terminals I1/I2, S1/S2 the sense terminals E1/E2. S1 senses the
P1 end. The package fails the build if a sense terminal shares a net with a force terminal or
with the other sense terminal: that would defeat the Kelvin connection (a 4-terminal part exists
so that no current-carrying copper sits between the sense pins). For a two-terminal use, take the
R2512 package instead.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Power", "Resistance")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "format_value")

Mpn = enum("WSK2512R0100FEA", "WSK2512R0100DEA", "WSK25125L000FEA")
mpn = config(Mpn, default="WSK2512R0100FEA", help="10 mOhm 1 % / 10 mOhm 0.5 % / 5 mOhm 1 %")

# Global Part Number Information: value and tolerance codes of each selectable part.
RESISTANCE = {
    "WSK2512R0100FEA": "10mOhm 1%",
    "WSK2512R0100DEA": "10mOhm 0.5%",
    "WSK25125L000FEA": "5mOhm 1%",
}

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)
S1 = io(Net)
S2 = io(Net)

resistance = Resistance(RESISTANCE[mpn.value])
power = Power("1W")  # Standard Electrical Specifications: P70 C

for s, name in [(S1, "S1"), (S2, "S2")]:
    check(
        s.name not in (P1.name, P2.name),
        f"WSK2512 {name} ({s.name}) shares a net with a force terminal: the Kelvin connection is lost",
    )
check(S1.name != S2.name, "WSK2512 S1 and S2 are on the same net")

Component(
    name="WSK2512",
    prefix="R",
    symbol=Symbol(library="WSK2512-HIGH.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("Vishay_WSK2512_6332Metric_5mR-200mR.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn=mpn.value, manufacturer="Vishay Dale"),
    pins={"I1": P1, "E1": S1, "E2": S2, "I2": P2},
    properties={
        "value": format_value(resistance, power),
        "package": "2512",
        "resistance": resistance,
        "power": power,
    },
    type="resistor",
)
